:"A certificate is secondary to actual contract drafting, rights analysis, IP research, and internship experience."}]}]},{"heading":"PG Options","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"LL.M"},{"type":"p","text":"Suitable specializations include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Intellectual Property Law"},{"text":"Media & Entertainment Law"},{"text":"Technology Law"},{"text":"Corporate Law"},{"text":"Commercial Law"},{"text":"International Business Law"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Other Options"},{"type":"p","text":"Depending on career direction:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MBA Media & Entertainment"},{"text":"MBA Marketing"},{"text":"MBA Business Management"},{"text":"Media Management"},{"text":"Entertainment Management"},{"text":"Technology & Innovation Management"},{"text":"For a specialist IP career, an LL.M in IP/Media/Technology Law can be particularly relevant."}]}]},{"heading":"Career Specializations","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"After gaining experience, the IP Associate can specialize in:"},{"type":"h","text":"Copyright Lawyer"},{"type":"p","text":"Film, music, publishing and digital content."},{"type":"h","text":"Trademark Lawyer"},{"type":"p","text":"Brand protection and enforcement."},{"type":"h","text":"Entertainment Lawyer"},{"type":"p","text":"Talent, production and distribution contracts."},{"type":"h","text":"Media Lawyer"},{"type":"p","text":"Broadcasting, digital media and content regulation."},{"type":"h","text":"IP Transactions Lawyer"},{"type":"p","text":"Licensing, assignments and commercialization."},{"type":"h","text":"IP Litigation Lawyer"},{"type":"p","text":"Copyright, trademark and related disputes."},{"type":"h","text":"Digital IP Lawyer"},{"type":"p","text":"OTT, creator economy, platforms and online content."},{"type":"h","text":"AI & IP Specialist"},{"type":"p","text":"AI-generated content, licensing and emerging IP issues."},{"type":"h","text":"Sports & Entertainment IP Specialist"},{"type":"p","text":"A